d on the stone. A substantial left margin is preserved at the start of each line. Unless the lines below were substantially further indented, there was no text below; the preserved vacat above line 1 (90mm)  is significantly greater than that between lines 1 and 2 (57mm), so it is unclear if another line originally stood above (the top of the stone appears intact) - if it did, it was either significantly above the preserved first line and/or indented several letters to the right.",{"_":48,"ana":49,"ref":50},{"ana":238},"#text_condition.incomplete",{"lettering":240,"dimensions":241},"Deep, very regular, v-cut letters, with a broad v-cut, hair-line extensions to wedge serifs, and a quite wide square module. The I in line one is extended.",[242,246,249],{"type":56,"l":243,"from":58,"to":58,"h":244,"unit":61,"atLeast":245,"atMost":245},"Line 1","68 (I = 87)","68",{"type":56,"l":247,"from":67,"to":67,"h":248,"unit":61,"atLeast":248,"atMost":248},"Line 2","58",{"type":65,"l":66,"from":58,"to":67,"h":250,"unit":61,"atLeast":250,"atMost":250},"57",{"_":252,"notBefore":176,"notAfter":72,"evidence":253},"First or second century","lettering",[255,257],{"_":75,"type":76,"ref":77,"corresp":256,"region":78},"#findspot",{"_":80,"type":81,"ref":82,"region":78},[259],[85,86],[],{"_":262,"role":91,"ref":263},"Teatro Romano di Catania","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/017",{"_":265,"mainLang":266,"languages":267},"Latin","la",[265],{"n":101,"url":269,"height":270,"width":271,"desc":272,"surfaceType":106},"ISic003420_tiled.tif","4080px","3072px","I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2024-03-19",[274,276,278],{"atLeast":275,"atMost":275},68,{"atLeast":277,"atMost":277},58,{"atLeast":279,"atMost":279},57,[115,281],"Manganaro, 1988, La Sicilia da Sesto Pompeo a Diocleziano",[120,283],"RZSFKACR",[285,286,287,28,32,288,125,126,127,128,126,289,29